              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "Series of photographs of a school of albacore tuna gathered by a seine net, off the Seychelles.</p><p> Albacore tuna, also known as yellowfin tuna, is a species of fish with a cosmopolitan distribution: in fact, it is found globally in the Western Atlantic, the Red Sea and the Indo-Pacific region (particularly in East Africa and around New Zealand). It evolves in schools in waters close to the surface, at temperatures ranging from 18 to 31°C.</p><p> This species measures an average of 150 cm when adult. Its vernacular name is due to the yellow color of its fins, clearly visible in the images.",
